Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:12:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 105/260] [ae-patch] Reorder sessions by drag in any Ordering,
 switching the sidebar to Manual

On 2026-10-20 Reid set upstream's project sort ("Sort projects by: Manual
order" in the Projects header menu) by mistake, since the session Manual
ordering sits behind the filter icon under Ordering, and then found that
dragging a session did nothing. He chose this fix: drag always works, and the
Move items always show in the row menu.

With the sidebar_grouping_ui view options on, the session lists publish
whenever they are listed (not while searching, not on the Archived display),
in every Ordering. Outside Manual, a drop on a row of the same list, or a
Move item, switches this device's Ordering to Manual with one toast saying
where to change it back, reads the saved order fresh, and then makes the
move. An empty saved order starts from the order the lists showed at the
move, so no other row moves, even coming from Status ordering; a saved order
from another device keeps its arrangement under the move. Moves made while
that read is pending wait behind it, so they apply in the order they were
made; leaving Manual first drops them, and a failed read drops them with the
existing error toast. Saves go through the existing queue with its revision
and one 409 replay. With the view options off nothing changes.

A row the saved order does not hold now shows above the ranked rows only
when it was created after the newest of them; an older row that loads late
(past the first page, or past 100 sessions) shows below the arranged rows
instead of jumping to the top. Ranking a move writes every loaded row in
where it shows, under the same rule, so a move still changes only the moved
row.

Drops on another list's rows keep their old behavior in every Ordering: a
pinned or archived row sees no row-order targets, so pinning, unpinning,
filing and unfiling drops are unchanged, and a drop across Triage groups
still does nothing. A drop on a row-order target is always consumed, so a
folder row dropped on a sibling never unfiles.
